d 'RISKCALPLOT': module to plot observed and model-predicted risks across values of discrete clinical scores
d
d      riskcalplot displays observed event risks and
d model-predicted risks across the distinct values of one to five
d discrete    clinical scores.	  For each score value, the
d observed risk is the proportion of observations with endpoint=1.
d Marker size is proportional to the	number of observations at
d that score value.    Unless noci is specified, each observed risk
d is accompanied by an exact Clopper-Pearson binomial confidence
d interval. The    confidence level is controlled by level().	 A
d separate regression model is fitted for each score. model(logit)
d fits a logistic risk function. model(log) fits a modified   
d Poisson model with a log link and robust standard errors.    The
d command uses a common complete-case analysis sample containing
d nonmissing values for the endpoint and every score	specified
d in the command. 
d
d KW: clinical scores
d KW: event risks
d KW: predicted risks
d
d Requires: Stata version 16
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260820
d
d Author: Suppachai Lawanaskol,  Chaiprakarn Hospital, Chiang Mai, Thailand
d Support: email suppachai.lawanaskol@@gmail.com
d
f riskcalplot.ado
f riskcalplot.sthlp
